// lexdb_exec: the audit's missing functions in the PostgreSQL door (design/lexdb-new-features.md P8, P15, P23): date_bin
// (strides of days, hours, seconds and fractions, origins before and after, a date, infinity, NULLs, grouped; 0A000, 22008),
// uuidv4, uuidv7 ([shift]), uuid_extract_version and uuid_extract_timestamp (versions 1, 4, 7, other variants), unistr (\XXXX,
// \+XXXXXX, \uXXXX, \UXXXXXXXX, surrogate pairs; 22025), encode and decode with PostgreSQL 19's base64url and base32hex,
// and the aggregates bit_and, bit_or, bit_xor and any_value (NULLs, empty input, DISTINCT, FILTER, OVER, 3,000 rows). Checked
// against PostgreSQL 19 (generated by tests/lexdb/gen_pg.py from newfn_queries.txt). Each answer: the columns' names and the
// rows, or the tag, or ERROR and the SQLSTATE; each statement runs with lexdb_batch off and on.
